1
00:00:01,265 --> 00:00:02,565
(Episode 26)

2
00:00:05,605 --> 00:00:07,135
Seriously, just tteokbokki?

3
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:09,175
What do you mean, "just?"

4
00:00:09,905 --> 00:00:11,405
It's been ten years since I last had this.

5
00:00:15,675 --> 00:00:17,845
I couldn't bring myself to eat tteokbokki all this time.

6
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:24,125
It brought back too many memories, so I couldn't stomach it.

7
00:00:25,985 --> 00:00:27,525
It felt like something was caught in my throat.

8
00:00:37,335 --> 00:00:38,335
It's delicious.

9
00:00:55,455 --> 00:00:56,515
Seok Jin, where are you?

10
00:00:57,255 --> 00:00:59,625
Oh, I'm just meeting with someone.

11
00:01:00,795 --> 00:01:01,795
Really?

12
00:01:07,095 --> 00:01:08,695
What's wrong? What happened?

13
00:01:08,995 --> 00:01:11,335
Seok Jin, I'm hurt.

14
00:01:12,235 --> 00:01:14,305
How did you get hurt? Are you okay?

15
00:01:14,775 --> 00:01:17,545
I'm at the office. Please come right away. Hurry.

16
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:20,915
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

17
00:01:27,755 --> 00:01:28,755
Was that Hae Ra?

18
00:01:31,025 --> 00:01:32,025
Yes.

19
00:01:33,925 --> 00:01:34,925
You have...

20
00:01:36,795 --> 00:01:38,025
to go, don't you?

21
00:01:44,305 --> 00:01:45,365
Are you going to?

22
00:01:49,705 --> 00:01:51,145
I think Hae Ra got hurt.

23
00:01:52,605 --> 00:01:54,315
I'm sorry. I have to go.

24
00:02:03,455 --> 00:02:05,125
Do you have to be the one to go?

25
00:02:10,895 --> 00:02:11,895
Just...

26
00:02:13,395 --> 00:02:14,665
Can't you just not go?

27
00:02:34,785 --> 00:02:35,785
I'm sorry.

28
00:03:07,815 --> 00:03:10,585
Director Joo, I need you to go to Hae Ra.

29
00:03:37,685 --> 00:03:38,685
Ko Eun Seol.

30
00:03:41,955 --> 00:03:42,955
Seok Jin.

31
00:03:53,665 --> 00:03:54,665
What about Hae Ra?

32
00:03:59,505 --> 00:04:00,575
Hold on a second.

33
00:04:06,605 --> 00:04:07,615
There you go.

34
00:04:10,785 --> 00:04:11,785
Let's go.

35
00:04:21,525 --> 00:04:24,125
Thanks to you, I really enjoyed the tteokbokki.

36
00:04:25,395 --> 00:04:26,995
You didn't even finish it.

37
00:04:31,635 --> 00:04:32,635
Oh, right.

38
00:04:33,935 --> 00:04:34,935
Go on inside.

39
00:04:35,435 --> 00:04:36,435
Okay.

40
00:04:41,175 --> 00:04:42,845
Listen, Seok Jin.

41
00:04:45,685 --> 00:04:49,185
Let's eat tteokbokki together again next time.

42
00:04:49,855 --> 00:04:51,655
I know a really good place.

43
00:04:55,195 --> 00:04:56,695
Sure, let's do that.

44
00:05:02,495 --> 00:05:03,505
Eun Seol.

45
00:05:06,005 --> 00:05:08,775
Attorney Seo, did you just get home from work?

46
00:05:09,435 --> 00:05:11,645
Yes, I had some things to take care of today.

47
00:05:15,475 --> 00:05:18,045
Chief Cha, what brings you here?

48
00:05:19,415 --> 00:05:21,185
I dropped her off on my way.

49
00:05:24,025 --> 00:05:25,025
I see.

50
00:05:27,425 --> 00:05:30,025
By the way, do you two live together?

51
00:05:30,195 --> 00:05:31,195
Gosh, no.

52
00:05:31,965 --> 00:05:34,065
Attorney Seo lives in the main house,

53
00:05:34,135 --> 00:05:35,465
and I live separately in the annex.

54
00:05:36,635 --> 00:05:38,265
When Eun Seol was looking for a place,

55
00:05:38,535 --> 00:05:40,375
our annex happened to be empty,

56
00:05:40,875 --> 00:05:43,505
so she's been staying there ever since.

57
00:05:47,175 --> 00:05:48,175
Is that so?

58
00:05:51,215 --> 00:05:52,485
Is everything comfortable?

59
00:05:53,655 --> 00:05:54,655
Yes.

60
00:05:54,785 --> 00:05:58,155
His sister makes me feel right at home, like my own sister.

61
00:06:00,625 --> 00:06:02,395
Eun Seol, aren't you going in?

62
00:06:03,155 --> 00:06:04,865
Right, I should.

63
00:06:07,335 --> 00:06:09,895
I'll see you at work then.

64
00:06:10,235 --> 00:06:11,235
Okay.

65
00:06:32,185 --> 00:06:33,185
What is all this?

66
00:06:34,695 --> 00:06:35,695
Are you okay?

67
00:06:36,055 --> 00:06:38,695
Why are you here? Where's Seok Jin?

68
00:06:38,865 --> 00:06:41,095
He said he had something urgent and asked me to come instead.

69
00:06:41,165 --> 00:06:43,195
- Are you hurt anywhere? - What the...

70
00:06:43,605 --> 00:06:44,635
Forget it.

71
00:06:45,705 --> 00:06:47,275
Is Cha Seok Jin out of his mind?

72
00:06:48,435 --> 00:06:49,475
What do you mean by that?

73
00:06:51,345 --> 00:06:53,145
Do you know who he's with right now?

74
00:06:53,875 --> 00:06:56,615
He's probably having dinner alone with Ko Eun Seol.

75
00:06:57,145 --> 00:06:59,285
Ko Eun Seol keeps hitting on Seok Jin,

76
00:06:59,285 --> 00:07:00,985
and he's falling for it.

77
00:07:01,185 --> 00:07:02,415
That annoying little...

78
00:07:03,255 --> 00:07:06,995
Is that why you put on this show and waited for Seok Jin?

79
00:07:07,455 --> 00:07:09,495
I had to do whatever it takes to make him come.

80
00:07:09,855 --> 00:07:11,595
Cha Seok Jin belongs right by my side.

81
00:07:13,425 --> 00:07:14,535
You know it too, right?

82
00:07:15,065 --> 00:07:16,935
Your feelings for Seok Jin are stronger than his for you.

83
00:07:18,665 --> 00:07:19,665
Director Joo...

84
00:07:20,205 --> 00:07:23,175
The more emotional you act, the lower your chances of winning.

85
00:07:23,745 --> 00:07:24,975
Then what should I do?

86
00:07:25,275 --> 00:07:26,545
Should I just sit around and wait?

87
00:07:27,645 --> 00:07:29,315
You need to find his weakness and use it against him.

88
00:07:30,485 --> 00:07:31,515
What's his weakness?

89
00:07:32,585 --> 00:07:33,585
Take a guess.

90
00:07:37,085 --> 00:07:38,085
Ms. Park?

91
00:07:40,395 --> 00:07:41,855
Hey, you're here.

92
00:07:42,455 --> 00:07:45,195
What took you so long? Who were you with, doing what?

93
00:07:46,395 --> 00:07:48,695
I had a prior engagement. Are you hurt anywhere?

94
00:07:49,435 --> 00:07:50,505
Not really.

95
00:07:50,565 --> 00:07:53,975
The vase shattered and startled her, but she wasn't hurt.

96
00:07:53,975 --> 00:07:55,105
Right, I see.

97
00:07:56,205 --> 00:07:57,205
Whatever.

98
00:07:57,745 --> 00:07:59,045
If you feel bad, you can take me home.

99
00:08:27,735 --> 00:08:28,805
Ko Eun Seol.

100
00:08:31,975 --> 00:08:32,975
Seok Jin.

101
00:08:50,325 --> 00:08:52,025
(Cheongma)

102
00:08:53,595 --> 00:08:55,895
I met with Jong Min and sorted things out.

103
00:08:56,335 --> 00:08:59,735
He begged me not to release the video,

104
00:09:00,675 --> 00:09:02,635
which only made me angrier.

105
00:09:03,845 --> 00:09:05,705
I see. That must've been tough.

106
00:09:07,145 --> 00:09:08,145
Anyway,

107
00:09:08,345 --> 00:09:10,785
thanks to you, we got past it without any issues.

108
00:09:12,445 --> 00:09:13,785
That being said,

109
00:09:14,955 --> 00:09:18,155
regarding the budget execution for the scholarship foundation,

110
00:09:19,055 --> 00:09:21,655
I'd like you to handle the audit.

111
00:09:23,025 --> 00:09:26,325
Isn't that a matter for the administrative finance team?

112
00:09:28,395 --> 00:09:30,835
I just want to leave it to someone I can trust.

113
00:09:32,035 --> 00:09:33,435
The more I work,

114
00:09:34,305 --> 00:09:35,775
the more I feel like there's no one in my corner.

115
00:09:37,245 --> 00:09:39,175
Everyone is just busy stabbing me in the back.

116
00:09:40,615 --> 00:09:41,615
Director Joo.

117
00:09:43,915 --> 00:09:46,685
Do you understand what I am saying?

118
00:09:48,655 --> 00:09:50,955
Yes, I'll handle it as requested.

119
00:09:56,255 --> 00:09:58,165
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

120
00:09:58,225 --> 00:10:00,595
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

121
00:10:01,965 --> 00:10:03,435
Honestly, Kang Young Hoon.

122
00:10:04,565 --> 00:10:08,475
It's no fun when you give in so easily.

123
00:10:10,645 --> 00:10:12,975
As it is a mass-market line, I believe we should...

124
00:10:13,045 --> 00:10:15,645
reduce costs by utilizing overseas OEMs.

125
00:10:16,075 --> 00:10:19,285
If we switch to local OEM production in Vietnam or Indonesia,

126
00:10:19,745 --> 00:10:23,255
we can cut costs by at least 40 percent.

127
00:10:23,755 --> 00:10:26,485
I think you are misunderstanding the term "mass-market."

128
00:10:27,085 --> 00:10:30,055
Simply cutting raw material costs to keep products cheap...

129
00:10:30,125 --> 00:10:32,125
isn't my definition of a mass-market strategy.

130
00:10:34,095 --> 00:10:35,665
What do you think, Mr. Cha?

131
00:10:36,365 --> 00:10:37,765
If we move production overseas,

132
00:10:37,765 --> 00:10:39,365
we won't be able to control the defect rate.

133
00:10:40,505 --> 00:10:43,675
Our principle at Shoejoy is 100 percent domestic production.

134
00:10:44,145 --> 00:10:45,575
The products we develop...

135
00:10:45,745 --> 00:10:48,615
are functional shoes enhanced with our exclusive technology.

136
00:10:49,015 --> 00:10:52,185
The manufacturing process itself must not allow any room for error.

137
00:11:00,625 --> 00:11:02,855
Did you have to humiliate me like that in front of everyone?

138
00:11:03,225 --> 00:11:04,895
What do you mean, Ms. Kang?

139
00:11:05,095 --> 00:11:08,535
You jumped to agree with Eun Seol and shot my idea down completely.

140
00:11:08,895 --> 00:11:11,235
You could have phrased it nicely.

141
00:11:11,505 --> 00:11:13,305
What was I supposed to phrase nicely?

142
00:11:13,535 --> 00:11:16,075
Your stance was totally wrong, so I had to correct it.

143
00:11:16,135 --> 00:11:18,105
How come Eun Seol is right and I'm not?

144
00:11:18,105 --> 00:11:19,105
Kang Hae Ra.

145
00:11:20,505 --> 00:11:21,745
We're at work.

146
00:11:21,815 --> 00:11:23,745
Keep your personal feelings out of this.

147
00:11:23,815 --> 00:11:26,515
You're the one making this personal for me.

148
00:11:26,515 --> 00:11:27,515
What?

149
00:11:29,915 --> 00:11:31,925
- Do you really not know? - Know what?

150
00:11:32,185 --> 00:11:33,325
Ko Eun Seol.

151
00:11:34,025 --> 00:11:35,625
Don't you know she likes you?

152
00:11:38,195 --> 00:11:40,365
That was all in the past, when we were young and naive.

153
00:11:40,635 --> 00:11:42,335
Those half-baked feelings are long gone.

154
00:11:44,465 --> 00:11:45,665
Are you sure...

155
00:11:46,365 --> 00:11:47,405
it's all in the past?

156
00:11:47,935 --> 00:11:49,435
Is that why you're acting like this?

157
00:11:53,075 --> 00:11:54,715
Let's have a meal with Ms. Park sometime.

158
00:11:54,975 --> 00:11:56,445
I got a gift for her.

159
00:11:58,345 --> 00:11:59,345
Whatever.

160
00:12:00,445 --> 00:12:01,455
I'll leave you to it.

161
00:12:11,125 --> 00:12:13,425
- Mom! - My gosh, you scared me.

162
00:12:13,895 --> 00:12:15,835
Why are you yelling like that?

163
00:12:20,675 --> 00:12:21,705
Where is it?

164
00:12:22,205 --> 00:12:23,235
Where's what?

165
00:12:23,535 --> 00:12:25,005
Where's the maternity handbook?

166
00:12:25,375 --> 00:12:27,915
Beats me. How would I know?

167
00:12:28,415 --> 00:12:31,845
Just be honest with me. Where did you put it?

168
00:12:32,215 --> 00:12:34,655
Fine, I sold it. Happy?

169
00:12:35,315 --> 00:12:36,715
I sold it,

170
00:12:37,455 --> 00:12:39,685
and I'll be using that money to finance the business for Eun Guk,

171
00:12:39,755 --> 00:12:41,595
our third-generation only son.

172
00:12:42,195 --> 00:12:43,195
Mom.

173
00:12:43,795 --> 00:12:44,825
We...

174
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:46,895
have to keep that safe.

175
00:12:47,535 --> 00:12:50,735
Later, when Eun Seol gets her life sorted out,

176
00:12:50,805 --> 00:12:53,165
she said she'll look for her birth mother.

177
00:12:53,235 --> 00:12:55,905
For her to do that, we need to keep that handbook safe.

178
00:12:56,205 --> 00:12:57,205
Well,

179
00:12:57,575 --> 00:12:59,205
whether she finds her or we find her,

180
00:12:59,675 --> 00:13:00,945
isn't it the same thing?

181
00:13:02,515 --> 00:13:05,585
I'm kindly finding her birth mother to save her the trouble,

182
00:13:06,015 --> 00:13:08,155
so Eun Seol should be grateful.

183
00:13:08,585 --> 00:13:09,885
Are you just going to find her?

184
00:13:10,185 --> 00:13:11,855
Is it really just about finding her?

185
00:13:11,925 --> 00:13:14,355
You'll demand money for raising Eun Seol.

186
00:13:16,125 --> 00:13:17,725
Do you want to fund Eun Guk's business...

187
00:13:18,365 --> 00:13:19,865
even if it means selling out Eun Seol?

188
00:13:20,265 --> 00:13:22,265
Yes, that's exactly what I'm going to do.

189
00:13:22,835 --> 00:13:24,735
Our Eun Guk's life has been a thorny path...

190
00:13:24,805 --> 00:13:26,765
ever since his mom died.

191
00:13:27,205 --> 00:13:29,735
Imagine how hard it was for him, not being able to settle down.

192
00:13:30,805 --> 00:13:31,905
With that money,

193
00:13:33,075 --> 00:13:34,615
I'm going to pave a smooth road...

194
00:13:35,175 --> 00:13:38,945
for our Eun Guk's future. Got it?

195
00:13:39,545 --> 00:13:40,545
Mom...

196
00:13:40,615 --> 00:13:41,655
Still, that's...

197
00:13:41,885 --> 00:13:42,885
Mom!

198
00:13:45,455 --> 00:13:46,485
A smooth road...

199
00:13:50,355 --> 00:13:51,765
Where should I put this?

200
00:13:53,195 --> 00:13:56,895
This is key evidence for finding Eun Seol's birth mother,

201
00:13:58,505 --> 00:13:59,905
so where should I hide it?

202
00:14:04,605 --> 00:14:06,305
Joo Mi Ran, was it?

203
00:14:07,615 --> 00:14:08,615
Oh, boy.

204
00:14:09,245 --> 00:14:11,845
Where am I supposed to find Joo Mi Ran?

205
00:14:28,395 --> 00:14:30,565
Come on in. Have a seat.

206
00:14:35,335 --> 00:14:38,475
This is for the cooperation on the social project you requested.

207
00:14:38,605 --> 00:14:40,505
Right, thank you.

208
00:14:43,545 --> 00:14:46,285
You must be busy preparing for the grand opening these days.

209
00:14:46,345 --> 00:14:49,255
Well, from on-site setup to inventory checks,

210
00:14:49,315 --> 00:14:51,025
everything's going smoothly.

211
00:14:53,325 --> 00:14:54,755
How's your mother doing?

212
00:14:58,195 --> 00:14:59,325
She's doing well.

213
00:14:59,965 --> 00:15:01,695
She's been having fun at the daycare center.

214
00:15:03,335 --> 00:15:04,335
Here.

215
00:15:04,735 --> 00:15:06,865
This is a program being held in the country,

216
00:15:07,475 --> 00:15:09,505
and I thought it'd be good for So Yeon.

217
00:15:09,905 --> 00:15:11,605
(Art and Body Care Program for PTSD Patients)

218
00:15:11,845 --> 00:15:14,075
Both the CEO and the Chairman...

219
00:15:14,615 --> 00:15:16,715
care a great deal about So Yeon's condition.

220
00:15:16,775 --> 00:15:17,845
You know that, right?

221
00:15:18,245 --> 00:15:19,285
Yes.

222
00:15:19,385 --> 00:15:20,955
I mean, why wouldn't they?

223
00:15:21,415 --> 00:15:24,385
Between launching the new brand and taking care of your sick mother,

224
00:15:24,725 --> 00:15:26,085
they're worried their future son-in-law...

225
00:15:26,155 --> 00:15:27,595
is going to wear himself out.

226
00:15:28,825 --> 00:15:30,755
My mother and I will definitely be there.

227
00:15:31,465 --> 00:15:32,465
Good.

228
00:15:32,695 --> 00:15:35,395
Since the Chairman is personally supporting you,

229
00:15:35,465 --> 00:15:36,695
please feel comfortable attending.

230
00:16:05,825 --> 00:16:06,825
There you go.

231
00:16:16,575 --> 00:16:17,575
Yes?

232
00:16:17,705 --> 00:16:19,705
The CEO just asked for you.

233
00:16:21,615 --> 00:16:23,115
Sure, I'll be right there.

234
00:16:31,185 --> 00:16:33,285
With the launch of Shoejoy,

235
00:16:34,255 --> 00:16:36,925
you have a lot to prove, Chief Cha.

236
00:16:38,465 --> 00:16:41,065
I'll do my best to ensure everything proceeds without issues.

237
00:16:41,395 --> 00:16:44,165
No. Doing your best isn't enough.

238
00:16:44,965 --> 00:16:46,535
The process doesn't matter.

239
00:16:47,135 --> 00:16:50,175
In this industry, you are judged by the results.

240
00:16:50,875 --> 00:16:52,805
The path forward with Cheongma backing you...

241
00:16:53,305 --> 00:16:55,415
won't always be smooth.

242
00:16:57,275 --> 00:17:00,815
At times, it will act as your strongest backing,

243
00:17:01,415 --> 00:17:02,455
but you must...

244
00:17:03,155 --> 00:17:05,625
fully endure the weight that comes with it first.

245
00:17:10,355 --> 00:17:12,395
I did the same, just so you know.

246
00:17:12,965 --> 00:17:16,065
This isn't a position you can get that easily.

247
00:17:19,505 --> 00:17:20,935
I'll be watching you.

248
00:17:22,735 --> 00:17:23,775
Understood, sir.

249
00:17:24,175 --> 00:17:25,805
I won't let you down.

250
00:17:27,615 --> 00:17:29,015
All right, you may go.

251
00:17:29,045 --> 00:17:30,745
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

252
00:17:40,555 --> 00:17:42,795
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

253
00:17:46,365 --> 00:17:49,595
This isn't a position you can get that easily.

254
00:17:56,305 --> 00:17:58,605
Did you raise inspection standards for Shoejoy?

255
00:17:59,445 --> 00:18:01,445
I will personally oversee the sample testing.

256
00:18:02,215 --> 00:18:04,645
(Head of Legal Affairs, Seo Hyun Jae)

257
00:18:13,825 --> 00:18:15,295
Listen, Seok Jin.

258
00:18:17,025 --> 00:18:21,065
Let's eat tteokbokki together again next time.

259
00:18:21,765 --> 00:18:23,695
I know a really good place.

260
00:18:27,005 --> 00:18:28,705
Sure, let's do that.

261
00:18:32,905 --> 00:18:35,915
(Head of Legal Affairs, Seo Hyun Jae)

262
00:18:41,055 --> 00:18:43,815
Eun Seol, would you like to have lunch together?

263
00:18:56,235 --> 00:18:57,235
You know, Eun Seol,

264
00:18:57,805 --> 00:19:00,135
it's incredible to watch you grow every day,

265
00:19:01,005 --> 00:19:02,975
and it makes me so proud.

266
00:19:04,545 --> 00:19:07,575
That's why I want to keep cheering you on.

267
00:19:15,485 --> 00:19:16,485
Sounds good.

268
00:19:22,795 --> 00:19:23,795
So, that day,

269
00:19:24,595 --> 00:19:28,435
you took Chief Cha out for a meal to show your gratitude?

270
00:19:29,065 --> 00:19:31,705
Yes. If it weren't for him,

271
00:19:31,765 --> 00:19:34,105
I wouldn't have been able to deliver my presentation properly.

272
00:19:35,235 --> 00:19:36,235
That's true.

273
00:19:39,975 --> 00:19:40,975
Eun Seol,

274
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:43,075
about that day...

275
00:19:43,815 --> 00:19:45,785
I think I was a bit hasty.

276
00:19:47,115 --> 00:19:48,115
What?

277
00:19:49,755 --> 00:19:52,725
I was so thrilled you won the design competition,

278
00:19:53,655 --> 00:19:55,355
and I just got caught up in the moment.

279
00:19:58,425 --> 00:20:00,125
I didn't consider how you felt...

280
00:20:01,025 --> 00:20:02,865
and only focused on my own feelings.

281
00:20:03,665 --> 00:20:05,865
Well, I have to admit...

282
00:20:06,635 --> 00:20:08,835
I was a little taken aback.

283
00:20:10,635 --> 00:20:11,905
It seemed like it.

284
00:20:14,045 --> 00:20:16,545
I don't want things to be awkward between us.

285
00:20:17,675 --> 00:20:20,745
If that's still bothering you...

286
00:20:22,955 --> 00:20:24,215
Please forget all about it, Eun Seol.

287
00:20:25,885 --> 00:20:28,625
Are you really okay with that?

288
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:31,165
My feelings matter too,

289
00:20:32,765 --> 00:20:35,265
but I don't want to make things uncomfortable for you.

290
00:20:38,605 --> 00:20:40,535
Thank you so much, Attorney Seo.

291
00:20:41,405 --> 00:20:45,375
To me, you're like my Daddy Long Legs.

292
00:20:46,075 --> 00:20:48,675
Always so comforting and reliable.

293
00:20:52,785 --> 00:20:54,955
I guess my legs are pretty long.

294
00:20:57,085 --> 00:21:00,225
Eun Seol, what if I were short?

295
00:21:01,425 --> 00:21:04,395
Would that make me Daddy Short Legs?

296
00:21:05,425 --> 00:21:07,595
Are you kidding me?

297
00:21:07,595 --> 00:21:08,695
You know...

298
00:21:09,235 --> 00:21:11,095
more like an Oompa-Loompa.

299
00:21:12,035 --> 00:21:13,465
Oompa loompa doompety doo

300
00:21:15,805 --> 00:21:17,175
I don't think that's how it goes.

301
00:21:23,345 --> 00:21:24,375
Ms. Ko.

302
00:21:34,855 --> 00:21:37,695
Go find some functional walking shoes from other brands.

303
00:21:38,095 --> 00:21:39,125
Oh, wait.

304
00:21:39,565 --> 00:21:40,625
Are they in storage?

305
00:21:41,335 --> 00:21:42,435
The storage room?

306
00:21:43,035 --> 00:21:45,235
Why? Is that a problem?

307
00:21:46,735 --> 00:21:49,205
No, I'll go get them.

308
00:21:55,375 --> 00:21:58,285
(Do Not Block Passageway)

309
00:22:05,325 --> 00:22:06,355
What are you doing out here?

310
00:22:09,355 --> 00:22:11,925
I need to find some samples in storage,

311
00:22:11,995 --> 00:22:13,925
but there's nothing to prop the door open with.

312
00:22:15,735 --> 00:22:17,535
Let's go in. I'll help you find them.

313
00:23:00,475 --> 00:23:02,875
Are you okay? You should be careful.

314
00:23:04,375 --> 00:23:05,385
Right.

315
00:23:05,945 --> 00:23:06,945
Thank you.

316
00:23:08,185 --> 00:23:09,185
Well...

317
00:23:09,985 --> 00:23:11,585
Are these what you're looking for?

318
00:23:13,125 --> 00:23:14,125
Yes.

319
00:23:20,225 --> 00:23:22,895
What is this? Why are you two together?

320
00:23:24,835 --> 00:23:26,605
We just happened to run into each other here.

321
00:23:27,835 --> 00:23:29,835
Why on earth would you be carrying this?

322
00:23:45,585 --> 00:23:47,555
I'm back.

323
00:23:47,995 --> 00:23:49,825
Hey, son.

324
00:23:51,765 --> 00:23:54,765
Hold on. Teun Teun, what's with your face?

325
00:23:54,835 --> 00:23:55,835
Did something happen?

326
00:23:56,035 --> 00:23:58,135
I just can't get Taegeuk 1 Jang right.

327
00:23:58,205 --> 00:23:59,435
I'm so bad at it.

328
00:24:01,835 --> 00:24:04,105
Seo Teun Teun, come on.

329
00:24:06,405 --> 00:24:08,375
Now, get ready for Taegeuk 1 Jang.

330
00:24:10,115 --> 00:24:11,215
Low block on one.

331
00:24:11,645 --> 00:24:12,785
Middle punch on two.

332
00:24:13,515 --> 00:24:16,015
Low block on one. Middle punch on two.

333
00:24:16,315 --> 00:24:18,255
Low block and middle punch.

334
00:24:20,085 --> 00:24:21,185
Lower your hand a bit more.

335
00:24:21,955 --> 00:24:25,165
The key to Taegeuk 1 Jang is getting the angles right.

336
00:24:25,465 --> 00:24:26,495
Follow me.

337
00:24:30,295 --> 00:24:32,405
See? That was great, Teun Teun.

338
00:24:32,605 --> 00:24:35,605
Uncle Jokbal, show me more.

339
00:24:35,675 --> 00:24:37,675
More!

340
00:24:40,475 --> 00:24:41,475
Watch the angle.

341
00:24:48,885 --> 00:24:50,215
Teun Teun, what are you up to?

342
00:24:52,185 --> 00:24:53,785
Working on your picture diary?

343
00:24:53,785 --> 00:24:54,795
Yes.

344
00:24:56,155 --> 00:24:57,195
"Playing father..."

345
00:24:58,265 --> 00:24:59,425
Playing father and son?

346
00:24:59,565 --> 00:25:04,705
Yes. I loved playing father and son with Uncle Jokbal today.

347
00:25:06,735 --> 00:25:08,375
Why is that playing father and son?

348
00:25:08,805 --> 00:25:09,905
Si Hoo and Min Chan...

349
00:25:09,975 --> 00:25:12,045
both said their dads taught them taekwondo.

350
00:25:12,675 --> 00:25:14,205
Today, Uncle Jokbal taught me taekwondo...

351
00:25:14,275 --> 00:25:15,775
like he was my dad.

352
00:25:16,645 --> 00:25:19,945
So with him, I was playing father and son.

353
00:25:21,785 --> 00:25:23,485
I'll ask him...

354
00:25:23,485 --> 00:25:25,585
to teach me again tomorrow, and the day after that.

355
00:25:37,665 --> 00:25:39,265
- Hyun Jae. - Yes?

356
00:25:40,065 --> 00:25:41,975
Can you do Taegeuk 1 Jang?

357
00:25:42,075 --> 00:25:43,575
Where is this coming from?

358
00:25:43,935 --> 00:25:46,375
Teun Teun's been practising taekwondo lately.

359
00:25:47,145 --> 00:25:48,815
I was hoping you could teach him a little.

360
00:25:49,315 --> 00:25:50,345
Taegeuk 1 Jang?

361
00:25:51,015 --> 00:25:52,985
Of course I forgot. How could I remember that?

362
00:25:54,045 --> 00:25:56,215
How can you not remember?

363
00:26:02,095 --> 00:26:03,095
What the...

364
00:26:05,025 --> 00:26:07,925
Director Joo, should we eat out today?

365
00:26:08,495 --> 00:26:09,495
Eat out?

366
00:26:09,565 --> 00:26:13,335
Yes. Young Hoon has dinner with Assemblyman Kim today.

367
00:26:13,805 --> 00:26:15,405
Let's grab dinner with Hae Ra before heading home.

368
00:26:15,475 --> 00:26:16,735
I already told her.

369
00:26:17,575 --> 00:26:19,605
Sounds good. I'll make a reservation.

370
00:26:20,805 --> 00:26:24,145
Oh, right. Should we ask Chief Cha to join us?

371
00:26:24,815 --> 00:26:27,145
I already asked, but he's going to be working late for a while.

372
00:26:27,415 --> 00:26:28,515
He must be really busy.

373
00:26:28,615 --> 00:26:30,855
Yes, he probably is.

374
00:26:30,915 --> 00:26:32,085
What a bummer.

375
00:26:33,285 --> 00:26:34,755
How about French tonight?

376
00:26:35,125 --> 00:26:36,595
Sounds great.

377
00:26:37,955 --> 00:26:39,095
Let's go.

378
00:26:44,165 --> 00:26:46,235
Oh my. Eun Seol!

379
00:26:48,475 --> 00:26:50,035
Were you still at the office?

380
00:26:50,235 --> 00:26:52,245
I still have some work left to do.

381
00:26:52,705 --> 00:26:55,415
Every new hire works late when they first start.

382
00:26:56,445 --> 00:26:57,475
Get back to it then.

383
00:26:58,585 --> 00:27:00,445
You haven't eaten yet, right?

384
00:27:00,985 --> 00:27:02,685
Would you like to have dinner with us?

385
00:27:03,315 --> 00:27:05,485
Mom, are you kidding me?

386
00:27:05,655 --> 00:27:07,055
She said she had work to do.

387
00:27:08,055 --> 00:27:11,225
She won't have any work left if you just sign off on it.

388
00:27:11,625 --> 00:27:14,165
You're her direct supervisor, after all.

389
00:27:14,865 --> 00:27:16,565
I guess that's true but...

390
00:27:17,695 --> 00:27:19,105
It'd be uncomfortable.

391
00:27:19,165 --> 00:27:20,535
Eating with her supervisor and her mom?

392
00:27:20,605 --> 00:27:21,875
Imagine how uncomfortable that would be.

393
00:27:22,975 --> 00:27:24,035
Right, Ko Eun Seol?

394
00:27:25,005 --> 00:27:28,575
Even so, I'd like to have a meal with you, Eun Seol.

395
00:27:29,345 --> 00:27:31,475
Would that make you too uncomfortable?

396
00:27:36,255 --> 00:27:38,755
No, I won't feel uncomfortable at all.

397
00:27:38,855 --> 00:27:40,125
Oh my, really?

398
00:27:40,685 --> 00:27:42,325
Then let's grab a bite together.

399
00:27:43,425 --> 00:27:45,325
Gosh, this is great.

400
00:27:57,135 --> 00:27:59,645
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

401
00:28:06,515 --> 00:28:08,355
Chief Cha, it's pretty late for a call.

402
00:28:08,615 --> 00:28:11,155
I'm reviewing the launch documents for Shoejoy.

403
00:28:11,385 --> 00:28:14,655
Could you check if there's any risk of a trademark dispute?

404
00:28:15,655 --> 00:28:16,795
Oh, I see.

405
00:28:17,155 --> 00:28:19,625
I'll start by looking into the core logo and slogan,

406
00:28:19,695 --> 00:28:22,235
and check for similar cases both domestically and internationally.

407
00:28:22,695 --> 00:28:23,735
Thank you. Then...

408
00:28:24,395 --> 00:28:25,435
Mr. Cha,

409
00:28:26,105 --> 00:28:28,475
are you free after work?

410
00:28:31,975 --> 00:28:33,075
Let's grab a drink.

411
00:28:41,715 --> 00:28:45,425
Thanks to you finding that flash drive the other day,

412
00:28:46,125 --> 00:28:48,495
Eun Seol was able to pull off her presentation successfully.

413
00:28:50,895 --> 00:28:52,795
It's a bit late, but thank you.

414
00:29:01,405 --> 00:29:04,475
Seeing Eun Seol make progress bit by bit...

415
00:29:05,445 --> 00:29:07,005
makes me more grateful than anything.

416
00:29:07,805 --> 00:29:10,545
Do you still feel that same guilt about Eun Seol?

417
00:29:11,945 --> 00:29:14,485
Of course I do. How could I not?

418
00:29:17,485 --> 00:29:21,555
It'll probably weigh on my heart for the rest of my life.

419
00:29:24,195 --> 00:29:25,195
The rest of your life?

420
00:29:28,125 --> 00:29:29,495
That level of guilt...

421
00:29:30,635 --> 00:29:32,305
Isn't that a burden to Eun Seol as well?

422
00:29:36,635 --> 00:29:37,975
If it weighs on you that much,

423
00:29:39,345 --> 00:29:41,845
putting it behind you might be the kindest thing for her.

424
00:29:44,945 --> 00:29:47,615
That's why I'm going to stay by her side and protect her.

425
00:29:49,055 --> 00:29:50,855
By her side, for the rest of my life.

426
00:29:53,555 --> 00:29:55,795
Do you think that's what she wants?

427
00:29:57,195 --> 00:29:58,565
I think she'd find it burdensome.

428
00:30:00,965 --> 00:30:01,965
If you ask me,

429
00:30:02,335 --> 00:30:04,365
you're the one becoming a burden to her.

430
00:30:09,935 --> 00:30:12,445
Aren't you engaged to Ms. Kang?

431
00:30:15,145 --> 00:30:16,645
Don't shake Eun Seol up...

432
00:30:17,445 --> 00:30:18,715
with your half-hearted sympathy.

433
00:30:20,445 --> 00:30:23,455
In the end, it will only hurt her.

434
00:30:32,525 --> 00:30:34,525
Eun Seol, you've been pretty busy lately, right?

435
00:30:34,595 --> 00:30:36,635
You're putting a lot of work into the new product development.

436
00:30:37,295 --> 00:30:40,405
The work is hard, but it's just as rewarding as it is fun.

437
00:30:40,465 --> 00:30:41,875
It's so fascinating...

438
00:30:41,875 --> 00:30:45,305
to see my sketches actually turn into real products.

439
00:30:45,575 --> 00:30:47,605
I sure am looking forward to it.

440
00:30:47,875 --> 00:30:50,175
If you keep up that positive mindset,

441
00:30:50,345 --> 00:30:52,285
there's no way the results won't turn out great.

442
00:30:53,545 --> 00:30:55,085
We won't know until we have the results.

443
00:30:58,115 --> 00:30:59,225
Excuse me.

444
00:31:08,365 --> 00:31:09,695
- Thank you. - Please enjoy.

445
00:31:12,405 --> 00:31:14,705
Let's eat while everything's warm.

446
00:31:15,275 --> 00:31:16,335
Right.

447
00:31:17,805 --> 00:31:20,105
It's been a while since we went out to eat together.

448
00:31:22,715 --> 00:31:23,745
Hold on.

449
00:31:24,445 --> 00:31:27,115
Eun Seol, can you not eat eggs?

450
00:31:31,085 --> 00:31:33,925
I'm allergic to egg whites.

451
00:31:34,185 --> 00:31:35,895
I haven't been able to eat them since I was little.

452
00:31:37,395 --> 00:31:38,395
Oh my.

453
00:31:38,725 --> 00:31:40,265
Me too.

454
00:31:40,695 --> 00:31:42,665
I'm also allergic to egg whites,

455
00:31:42,735 --> 00:31:45,405
so I haven't eaten eggs since I was young.

456
00:31:47,165 --> 00:31:49,235
We have quite a lot in common.

457
00:31:50,705 --> 00:31:51,905
I find it delicious.

458
00:32:05,755 --> 00:32:07,755
(Episode 27 airs September 16 at 7:50pm.)

459
00:32:33,415 --> 00:32:37,255
(A Trap Called Desire)

460
00:32:37,315 --> 00:32:40,785
I was thinking about this while eating with Eun Seol yesterday.

461
00:32:40,855 --> 00:32:43,695
What nonsense are you up to now?

462
00:32:43,755 --> 00:32:45,465
Don't you care about the group's image?

463
00:32:45,525 --> 00:32:48,195
I was surprised because I'd never seen that side of you.

464
00:32:48,265 --> 00:32:49,435
Are they dating?

465
00:32:49,435 --> 00:32:51,135
All signs point to that.

466
00:32:51,195 --> 00:32:52,905
They're always attached at the hip.

467
00:32:52,965 --> 00:32:55,405
Director Joo, I can trust you, right?

468
00:32:55,775 --> 00:32:56,775
Shopping?

469
00:32:57,175 --> 00:32:59,675
But I hate hanging out with Ms. Park.

470
00:32:59,945 --> 00:33:02,945
Consider today a special date for you and Hae Ra.

471
00:33:03,015 --> 00:33:04,715
Hello, this is Joo Mi Ran.

472
00:33:04,715 --> 00:33:06,245
Who is this?
